d Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Council","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Children's Services Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-08-12","committee":"Regeneration and Environment Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"West Yorkshire Pension Fund Advisory Panel","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Executive","time":"10.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Corporate Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Regeneration and Environment Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Bradford Council's \u00a3113m spending overspend funded by government emergency support","lead":"Bradford Council's accounts for 2025\u201326 have received an unqualified audit opinion, but the council ran a \u00a3113 million overspend on day-to-day spending, which was funded through a Capitalisation Direction\u2014emergency government permission to treat day-to-day spending as if it were capital spending. The overspend was \u00a314 million better than initially forecast, but the result is that the council did not meet its running costs from its own revenues. Usable reserves rose by \u00a355 million to \u00a3229.2 million, largely because costs funded by the Capitalisation Direction were earmarked in reserves rather than charged directly to spending. The General Fund balance stands at \u00a353.1 million, equivalent to 3.5 per cent of the council's gross expenditure.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Doc N - Covering Report External Audit Completions 2025-26 for GAC 24 September 2026","paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57378/57378.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Bradford Council accounts pass audit despite \u00a3113m revenue shortfall","lead":"Bradford Council's accounts for 2025-26 received an unqualified audit opinion despite day-to-day spending exceeding income by \u00a3113 million. The overspend was \u00a314m better than forecast and was funded through a Capitalisation Direction, emergency government permission allowing councils to finance revenue gaps by borrowing. The council's usable reserves\u2014money set aside\u2014increased by \u00a355m to \u00a3229.2m, providing stronger financial cushioning. The council's pension fund audit identified \u00a360.9m in valuation errors among highly subjective investments but the auditor anticipates issuing an unqualified opinion pending completion of outstanding work.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Doc N - Covering Report External Audit Completions 2025-26 for GAC 24 September 2026","paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57378/57378.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Doc Q - COBMDC - Internal Audit Strategy and 2026-27 Annual Plan - FINAL post CMT","paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57376/57376.pdf","headline":"\u00a346 million annual highways grant income requires compliance audit verification","detail":"The Highways Department received \u00a346 million in grant income in 2025-26 and a 30-day priority audit is planned to verify compliance with grant conditions. This indicates material grant dependency and recognition of clawback risk.","category":"income","matters":"Significant grant dependency creates clawback and cash flow risk if compliance fails; audit focus indicates the council treats this as a control priority.","figures":"\u00a346 million grant income to Highways in 2025-26","quote":"the Highways Department received \u00a346million in grant income in 2025-26. We will audit the Department's arrangements for compliance with grant conditions.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Doc Q - COBMDC - Internal Audit Strategy and 2026-27 Annual Plan - FINAL post CMT","paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57376/57376.pdf","headline":"Workforce cost control audits planned for agency workers, overtime, and sickness absence","detail":"Workforce identified as a strategic risk category. Priority audits allocate 30 days to agency worker management and 30 days to overtime payment controls; an indicative 40-day audit of sickness absence management is also planned, indicating management concern about labor cost control.","category":"people","matters":"Labor costs are typically material to council budgets; multiple focused audits on agency workers and overtime suggest management concern about cost control or compliance in discretionary spend areas.","figures":"Agency workers audit: 30 days; Overtime: 30 days; Sickness absence audit (indicative): 40 days","quote":"Use of Agency Workers- we will audit the Council's arrangements for the management and payment of agency worker staff.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Doc Q - COBMDC - Internal Audit Strategy and 2026-27 Annual Plan - FINAL post CMT","paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57376/57376.pdf","headline":"Financial Resilience & Sustainability established as a primary strategic risk driving audit planning","detail":"The council's August 2026 risk assessment identifies Financial Resilience & Sustainability as one of 14 strategic risk categories. Multiple priority audits are mapped to this risk category including cash and treasury management, property and asset management, scheme of delegation, and agency worker controls.","category":"governance","matters":"The council's own risk assessment identifies financial sustainability as requiring targeted audit and management attention; this signals to a lender how the council rates its own financial resilience.","figures":"Financial Resilience & Sustainability one of 14 strategic risks; 7 priority audits mapped to this risk category","quote":"The Council's risk profile as at August 2026 included 14 risk categories as outlined below:","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Doc Q - COBMDC - Internal Audit Strategy and 2026-27 Annual Plan - FINAL post CMT","paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57376/57376.pdf","headline":"Bradford Children's & Families Trust identified as strategic sustainability risk but excluded from audit scope","detail":"Internal audit explicitly provides assurance to the council and WYPF only, with BCFT and other subsidiaries not audited. Yet BCFT is listed as one of 14 strategic risk categories (BCFT \u2013 Sustainability), creating a governance gap where a subsidiary carrying identified sustainability risk lacks independent assurance oversight.","category":"governance","matters":"A subsidiary carrying a named sustainability risk operates without internal audit oversight, limiting visibility of control effectiveness or financial distress indicators.","figures":"BCFT identified as one of 14 strategic risks; audit coverage explicitly excludes it and other subsidiaries","quote":"IA currently provides audit services to the Council and WYPF but not to BCFT or other subsidiaries.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Doc Q - COBMDC - Internal Audit Strategy and 2026-27 Annual Plan - FINAL post CMT","paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57376/57376.pdf","headline":"Audit function carrying 5 vacancies with only 30 days contingency, limiting governance assurance delivery","detail":"The internal audit team has 5 unfilled vacancies acting as a limiting factor on audit volume. Resource availability (650 days) barely exceeds requirement (620 days), leaving only 30 days contingency to respond to emerging risks or priority changes. All planned audits target completion by end April 2027.","category":"governance","matters":"Governance and control oversight depend on adequate assurance capacity; constrained audit resources limit the council's ability to identify and remediate control weaknesses or emerging risks.","figures":"5 vacancies; 620 days required; 650 days available; 30 days contingency","quote":"The audit team is currently carrying 5 vacancies which acts as a limiting factor on the volume of audits which can be delivered.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Bradford","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-24","since_iso":"2026-08-25","distress":true,"headline":"\u00a346 million annual highways grant income requires compliance audit verification","lead":"Significant grant dependency creates clawback and cash flow risk if compliance fails; audit focus indicates the council treats this as a control priority.","also":["29 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Governance and Audit Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":30,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Doc Q - COBMDC - Internal Audit Strategy and 2026-27 Annual Plan - FINAL post CMT","top_paper_url":"https://bradford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57376/57376.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":98,"news_drafts_total":2}}